      "Title": "JeremyAnsel.DirectX.MediaFoundation.MFSample",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/JeremyAnsel.DirectX.MediaFoundation.MFSample.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">The IMFSample interface represents a multimedia sample for a\nmultimedia stream type.  An typical example is a video frame,\nand a notable exception is audio where an IMFSample does not usually\nrepresent a single sample of audio, but rather a chunk\nof audio samples.  Note that this allows us to reduce the overhead for\nrepresenting audio in the pipeline.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/JeremyAnsel.DirectX.MediaFoundation.MFSample.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"8\">A sample may consist of a multiple buffers as is the case of compressed\naudio or video samples received from the network or being sent to an\nASF media sink or ASF multiplexer.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/JeremyAnsel.DirectX.MediaFoundation.MFSample.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"12\">The IMFAttributes interface can be used to tag the sample with extra\ninformation that is not represented by the IMFSample methods.\nThe MFSampleExtension_xxx GUIDs in mfapi.h define some standard\nattributes, but custom attributes are allowed and are preserved\nthrough the Media Foundation pipeline as well as possible.</p>\n"
    },
